<title>USA: Registry Q2 pro forma shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Registry Q2 pro forma shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEWTON, Mass. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.14   profit	 $0.11</p>
<p> Net loss		   1,208   profit	 1,858</p>
<p> Revs			75,091		   48,191</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  12,543		   10,870</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.13   profit	 $0.22</p>
<p> Net profit		 2,675   profit	 3,575</p>
<p> Revs		     144,520		   94,532</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,599		   10,867</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Q2 1996 results are pro forma to account for the acquisitions of five companies, two of which are accounted for as a pooling of interests and resulted in a one-time charge of $4.9 million. The pro forma results reflect the combined results of the Registry and the two companies.</p>
<p>Full company name is Registry Inc</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
